A||N||10||terryk||Fiero SC - First Thoughts By Terry Kelley||||14||
Z||000000||terryk||10-28-2000||12:51 AM||||I got to drive the Fiero SC tonight for the first time at any length (or throttle position). For the record, this is a 92 Park Avenue Ultra 92 Buick 3800 SC with a 4T60E in an 86 SE. Stock ECM calibrations. <P>Surprisingly, it is extremely well behaved. I expected it to be a bit squirrely, but in fact it launches very nice (courtesy of anti abuse). The shifts are a dream. No lurching or banging. Upshifts and downshifts are the stock silky smooth. I might tighten them up a bit.<P>100 MPH clicks off very fast. No times yet, but it's certainly not a stock Fiero anymore.  The rear doesn't go all wonky as I suspected it might. It stays nice a straight (although I did discover just how much the rear camber/toe affects the front wheels. A little goes a long way).<P>To me it went from being a nice cruising car to a very solid fast cruising car. <P>Well, the next items are to bolt the 94 blower and TB on there and make some calibration changes. There are some cleanup's to do, but it's pretty much done.<P>I want to thank those that helped me out on this. Starcher, FieroBob (fastest mail in the west), Hypnotise, the effervescent Ludis, Theogre, Masterful80, Cooter and a few others I can't recall right now. I'll return the favor.<P>Terry<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-29-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||mrfixit58||10-28-2000||09:45 AM||||Congratulations Terry,<P>I wish I had one!<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
