Z||000003||terryk||10-28-2000||02:05 PM||||Funny, I've given that some thought. The Ciera feels like 100MPH. Strange, but the Fiero doesn't.||||reg||14
Z||000004||stimpy||10-28-2000||03:55 PM||||Man, that Ciera SC 3800 sounds like a blast.  I had an 87 Ciera Brougham 4 door with the series 1 3.8 in it and was it ever a sleeper. It was my (grand)fathers Oldsmobile, and definately looked the part.  I can only imagine the fun of dusting off some "fast" cars in such a grandpa looking car.  Maybe next time I make it to CA I could come check it out. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||10-28-2000||06:32 PM||||Hi Stimpy,<P>I guess the Ciera is a bit of sleeper but it's a Ciera GT and the front and rear facia are different. It has the GT logos and I added the "Supercharged" emblems on the front in place of "Fuel Injected".<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/r0300063.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||10-28-2000||11:59 PM||||Cool. I bet that's a great car to blast I-5 with.  Mine had an unfortunate problem that when some stereo shop butcher went to install the alarm, he broke the dashboard. Therefore it shivered like a wet, nervous chihuahua over 70 mph.  Other then that it was a great car.  Have you evr considered putting in the flush headlamps like were on my 87 Brougham?||||reg||1
