Z||000009||Mark O'Hara||10-29-2000||10:58 PM||||Terry,<BR>How much trouble was it to mount the transmission on the subframe and did you have to make new axles or did you find the lengths you needed from something else?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Mark||||reg||1
Z||000010||terryk||10-30-2000||12:41 AM||||I used 94 A car axles (it came with the 4T60E) and swapped Fiero manual trans outer CV's in. The manual trans Fiero axles are the same size as the A car axles. I talked to several places and they said they would supply this combo for ~$80/axle. 92-97 U-van with the 3800/4T60E axles seem to be the same as the 94 and up A-car (Ciera/6000/Century). Again, the outer CV's from a manual trans Fiero are needed.<P>I used A-car transmission mounts and brackets from a 4T60/440/4T60E. The cradle had to be slotted to the right just like the rear slots. The rear has two sets of slots. Just copy that on the front.<P>I used Chris Wests engine bracket and an A-car engine mount. This was the only custom part. The axles are just combined pieces.||||reg||1
